# MSBuild reads this file for every build whose entry project lies under tests/ (`dotnet build` or `dotnet test` of one
# suite), and passes its switches as global properties to that project and every project it references. The suites read
# and edit SPIR-V (binding reflection, reload refusals), so a suite's build plans SPIR-V on Windows too, as a solution
# build does (build/Shaders.targets).
-p:PuckShaderSpirvEnabled=true
